data: {"content_index":0,"item_id":"item_REDACTED_274","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":278,"text":"Let \\(t\\) = time (in hours) after Train 1 leaves Station A until they meet.\n\n- Train 1 speed: \\(60\\text{ km/h}\\)  \n  Distance traveled: \\(60t\\)\n\n- Train 2 leaves \\(0.5\\) h later, speed \\(90\\text{ km/h}\\)  \n  Time traveled: \\(t-0.5\\)  \n  Distance traveled: \\(90(t-0.5)\\)\n\nThey start 300 km apart and move toward each other, so:\n\n\\[\n60t + 90(t-0.5)=300\n\\]\n\n\\[\n60t + 90t - 45 = 300\n\\]\n\n\\[\n150t = 345\n\\]\n\n\\[\nt = \\frac{345}{150}=2.3\\text{ h}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2.3\\text{ h} = 2\\text{ h }18\\text{ min}\n\\]\n\nSo they meet **2 hours 18 minutes after Train 1 leaves Station A**  \n(or **1 hour 48 minutes after Train 2 leaves Station B**).\n\nDistance from Station A:\n\n\\[\n60 \\times 2.3 = 138\\text{ km}\n\\]\n\n✅ They meet **138 km from Station A**.","type":"response.output_text.done"}

